==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}}, from {{proto|Germanic|spīwanan|lang=is}}, whence also German {{term|speien|lang=de}}, Englih ''[[spew]]'', Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍀𐌴𐌹𐍅𐌰𐌽|tr=speiwan|lang=got}}. Non-Germanic cognates include Old Armenian {{term|թուք||tr=tʿukʿ|lang=xcl}}, Persian {{term|تف||spittle|tr=tuf|lang=fa}}, Ossetian {{term|ту||spittle|lang=os}}, Ancient Greek {{term|πτύω||I spit out|tr=ptuō|lang=grc}}, Latin {{term|spuo|lang=la}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|пльвати||lang=cu}} (Russian {{term|плевать|lang=ru}}) and Sanskrit {{term|ष्ठीवति|tr=ṣṭhīvati||to spit|lang=sa}}.

===Verb===
'''spýja'''

# to [[vomit]]

